Ok, given
```php
class A {
  public function foo(string $s) : string {
    return $s;
  }
}
```

Psalm will treat

```php
/** @method stdClass foo(stdClass $s) */
class B extends A {}
```

identically to

```php
class B extends A {
  /**
   * @param stdClass $s
   * @return stdClass
   */
  public function foo(string $s) : string {
    return parent::foo($s);
  }
}
```

issue.body:
Please see this code:

```php
interface ServiceInterface {}

class ConcreteService implements ServiceInterface {
    public function getById(int $i) : void {}
}

class Foo
{
    /** @var ServiceInterface */
    protected $service;

    public function __construct(ServiceInterface $service)
    {
        $this->service = $service;
    }
}

/** @property ConcreteService $service */
class FooBar extends Foo
{
    public function __construct(ConcreteService $concreteService)
    {
        parent::__construct($concreteService);
    }

    public function doSomething(): void
    {
        $this->service->getById(123);
    }
}
```

We get this error reported:

```php
ERROR: UndefinedInterfaceMethod - app/Demo/test.php:31:25 - Method ServiceInterface::getbyid does not exist
        $this->service->getById(123);
```

But the `@property` at the beginning of class `FooBar` declares the type of the property correctly.  And `ConcreteService` has the method `getById()`.
